## [Unreleased] - 2026-11-19

### Added

- `combine_tensor_patches` reuses one spatial overlap-count map across batches and channels, reducing reconstruction time and temporary tensor allocations without changing the overlap average. ([#6802](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6802))
- `kornia.feature.CLIDD` and `kornia.feature.CLIDDModel` port CLIDD (Cross-Layer Independent Deformable Description, arXiv:2601.09230), a family of nine very small learned local features with 48-, 64- or 128-D descriptors, from 4,252 to 4.4 M parameters. `CLIDD.from_pretrained(variant)` loads the authors' weights, `CLIDD(images)` returns keypoints, scores and descriptors per image, and `CLIDD.match` matches two images by the authors' dual-softmax mutual nearest neighbours. The authors' Triton kernels are optional: the descriptor sampling also runs as `grid_sample` plus a convolution on any device, matching them to float32 rounding, and `use_triton` selects the implementation (by default Triton for the 128-D variants on CUDA from torch 2.7, where it is faster and holds far less memory). ([#6805](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6805))
- SOLD2 local heatmap refinement batches overlapping blocks and ranks only active blocks, reducing per-block host synchronization while preserving thresholds, normalization and inactive blocks. Temporary memory scales with the covered block area; CUDA overlap sums may vary in the last bit. ([#6807](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6807))
- `crop_by_indices` copies identical exact-size crops as a batch, avoiding per-image slicing in eager `RandomCrop(same_on_batch=True)` while preserving contiguous, independent output tensors and image gradients. ([#6812](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6812))
- `AugmentationSequential` no longer builds the transformation matrix of each child on every call. Children whose matrix is lazy (flips, resizes, `RandomResizedCrop` in its default slice mode, and intensity augmentations) keep it lazy inside the container, and the chained matrix is built from the recorded calls when `.transform_matrix` is first read. Outputs, matrices, boxes, keypoints and masks are unchanged. On CUDA (Tesla T4, torch 2.11) with 224x224 images, a `RandomResizedCrop`, `RandomHorizontalFlip`, `ColorJitter`, `RandomGrayscale`, `Normalize` pipeline takes 31%, 15% and 11% less time at batch 16, 32 and 64 (12.1 to 8.4 ms at batch 16), and `RandomResizedCrop`, `RandomHorizontalFlip`, `RandomAffine` takes 31%, 28% and 24% less. ([#6816](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6816))
- Lovasz hinge loss sorts target labels without allocating a repeated batch-index tensor, saving 8 bytes per input pixel while preserving values and gradients. ([#6819](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6819))

### Bug fixes

- `rgb_to_xyz`, `xyz_to_rgb`, `rgb_to_yuv`, `yuv_to_rgb` and the Lab/Luv conversions built on them now compute float32 input in float32 on CUDA regardless of cuDNN's TF32 setting. With older cuDNN (for example torch 2.5.1) some shapes, and `torch.compile`, returned TF32-precision results. CPU results are unchanged. ([#6768](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6768))
- `mean_average_precision` computes detection counts, precision and recall in at least float32. Float16 and bfloat16 box inputs keep their output dtype but no longer receive AP credit for recall thresholds reached only by rounding; for example, 512 detections of 513 objects in bfloat16 score approximately 0.9102 instead of 1. ([#6803](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6803))
- `transform_points` now divides every nonzero homogeneous coordinate directly, so finite Euclidean points stay the
  same for nonzero scalar multiples of a projective matrix whose homogeneous products remain representable. The same
  change reaches `warp_grid`, `warp_grid3d`, `homography_warp` and `homography_warp3d` through those grids, and the
  traced `warp_perspective` grid. This replaces the undivided numerator returned when a scaled `w` was smaller than
  `1e-8`. Direct division can change projective results with `w != 1` at rounding level; affine results with `w = 1`
  remain bitwise unchanged. ([#6814](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6814))
- `RandomDissolving` now returns an empty image batch without running the diffusion model. ([#6815](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6815))
- `otsu_threshold` now counts histogram populations in int64 before normalization, preventing an incorrect threshold when a float32 histogram bin contains more than `2**24` pixels. ([#6818](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6818))
- `distort_points` and `undistort_points` with 14 coefficients, and `tilt_projection`, no longer compute the sensor-tilt products in half precision inside a caller's `torch.autocast` region, which moved points in a 640 x 480 image by up to 2 px in bfloat16. TorchScript calls keep the caller's precision. ([#6822](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6822))
- `crop_by_indices` retains the image gradient link for empty batches, fixing backward through empty slice-mode `CenterCrop2D`, `RandomCrop`, and `RandomResizedCrop` calls. ([#6823](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6823))
- `euler_from_quaternion`, `quaternion_from_euler`, `Se2.trans`, `Se3.trans`, `Vector2`, `Vector3`, `Vector2.from_coords`, `Vector3.from_coords`, `Hyperplane.signed_distance`, `Hyperplane.through` and `motion_from_essential_choose_solution` name the arguments and the shapes or types they got when a shape or type check fails, instead of the generic `Validation condition failed`. They still raise `BaseError`. ([#6828](https://github.com/kornia/kornia/pull/6828))
- `spatial_gradient3d` scales its first-order difference buffer in place, avoiding a second output-sized allocation while preserving input values and gradients.



